    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is derived from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), so I exposed it as a read-only response field computed at mapping time \u2014 no changes to the entity, service, or persistence layer.\n\n**Two files touched:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation to `toOwnerDto` plus a small, self-contained `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {\n       if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n           return null;\n       }\n       return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- I put the logic in `OwnerMapper` (a small interface, low `WMC_other`) rather than in `Owner` (a large class whose ~35 combined CC would multiply every edit).\n- The behaviour is a new, cohesive single-CC-branch helper; the only existing method changed is `toOwnerDto`, which gets one annotation line.\n- The null guard makes it correct even for seed owners (whose `customer_code`/`registration_date` are `NULL`), avoiding NPEs while producing `SMI-0007-M26`-style values for created owners (`year % 100`, zero-padded to two digits).",
